// Copy this file to `Local.xcconfig` (gitignored) to override the signing
// defaults in `Auger.xcconfig` and `AugerTopShelf.xcconfig`. Use this when
// signing with your own Apple Developer team rather than the default
// `com.artic0din.auger` identifiers and `group.com.artic0din.auger` App Group.
//
// Every target xcconfig ends with `#include? "Local.xcconfig"`, so any
// variable you redefine here wins. Each target reads its own indirection
// variable (`AUGER_TV_BUNDLE_ID` / `AUGER_TOPSHELF_BUNDLE_ID` plus the
// `_ENTITLEMENTS` variables), so you can change one target without affecting
// the other.
//
// After editing, run `xcodegen generate` from `iosApp/` and pick your
// team in Xcode's Signing & Capabilities tab.
//
// ----- Bundle IDs ---------------------------------------------------------
//
// Personal Teams cannot register identifiers that another team already owns,
// so give each target a unique prefix. Top Shelf must be prefixed by
// `AUGER_TV_BUNDLE_ID` or embedded-binary validation fails at install:
//
// AUGER_TV_BUNDLE_ID       = com.example.auger
// AUGER_TOPSHELF_BUNDLE_ID = com.example.auger.topshelf
//
// ----- Entitlements -------------------------------------------------------
//
// Personal Teams cannot join App Groups or use the User Management
// entitlement. Both the tvOS app and Top Shelf need the stripped
// `.personal.entitlements` variants:
//
// AUGER_TV_ENTITLEMENTS       = Auger.personal.entitlements
// AUGER_TOPSHELF_ENTITLEMENTS = TopShelf/TopShelf.personal.entitlements
// SILO_USER_INDEPENDENT_KEYCHAIN = NO
//
// Note: Top Shelf to host-app state handoff uses the App Group, so Apple TV
// Home Screen Top Shelf rows stay empty under a Personal Team. Everything
// else (playback, auth, library browsing) works.
//
// ----- Development team ---------------------------------------------------
//
// Optional — normally picked in Xcode's UI. Set here if you want every
// clean regenerate to come up pre-selected to your team:
//
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345
